    "result_text": "Done. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the build passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe membership-level logic lived in a single method, `membershipLevel(Owner)`, in `OwnerMapper.java`. I changed only that one method in that one file.\n\n**What changed** (`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`):\n- Added tenure as the factor that unlocks level 4: `+1` when the owner's tenure exceeds 365 days (i.e. `registrationDate` is more than 365 days before today).\n- Raised the cap from 3 to 4.\n- Updated the doc comment.\n\nBecause a newly created owner has zero tenure, that fourth increment never fires for them, so a new owner with an email (+1) and `namesakeCount == 0` (+1) tops out at level 3 \u2014 exactly what the spec and `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` require. Only owners registered over a year ago can reach level 4.\n\n**Structural impact kept low:**\n- One file touched, one function edited.\n- The new logic is a single independent `if` branch (CC +1) plus the cap constant \u2014 no new fields, no restructuring, no coupling to household/namesake code beyond what was already there.\n- I inlined the tenure check with fully-qualified `java.time.LocalDate` (matching the existing style in this file's mapping expressions) rather than adding a new helper class \u2014 a second file would have multiplied the total cost.\n\nFull test suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
